Description: virtual FIDO2 security key backed by TPM 2.0 and a fingerprint reader
 tpm-fido is a FIDO2/WebAuthn authenticator for Linux. It creates a virtual
 FIDO2 HID device through /dev/uhid that browsers use like a hardware security
 key.
 .
 Private keys are generated and stored in the TPM 2.0. User verification is
 performed with the fingerprint reader through fprintd. The daemon is provided
 as a systemd user service that runs in daemon mode with a system tray icon.
